1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,841
Mix blue paint with yellow
paint, and you get green.

2
00:00:03,841 --> 00:00:06,898
Stir milk into tea, and
it is one new colour.

3
00:00:06,898 --> 00:00:10,404
A grey sky is not white one
minute and black the next.

4
00:00:10,804 --> 00:00:12,237
A mix is not a switch.

5
00:00:12,237 --> 00:00:14,299
Some molecules are exactly like that.

6
00:00:14,749 --> 00:00:16,745
Diya stirs milk into her tea.

7
00:00:16,745 --> 00:00:21,288
In class, she drew ozone, O three,
with one double bond and one single

8
00:00:21,288 --> 00:00:22,188
bond.

9
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:24,232
But a double bond is shorter.

10
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:27,518
So one side should be
short, and one side long.

11
00:00:27,518 --> 00:00:30,286
The teacher said both sides are the same.

12
00:00:30,286 --> 00:00:31,186
How?

13
00:00:31,294 --> 00:00:34,793
By the end, you will see why one drawing
is not enough for some molecules.

14
00:00:35,443 --> 00:00:37,444
First, what is a Lewis structure?

15
00:00:37,444 --> 00:00:39,505
It is a dot drawing of a molecule.

16
00:00:39,505 --> 00:00:41,591
Lines show shared pairs of electrons.

17
00:00:41,941 --> 00:00:45,001
For some molecules, two or more
good drawings are possible.

18
00:00:45,001 --> 00:00:46,406
Same atoms, same places.

19
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:48,211
Only the electrons sit differently.

20
00:00:48,561 --> 00:00:52,686
Each drawing is called a canonical
structure, or a resonance structure.

21
00:00:52,686 --> 00:00:55,155
We join them with a double headed arrow.

22
00:00:55,505 --> 00:01:00,197
The real molecule is a mix of all of
them, like green from blue and yellow.

23
00:01:00,197 --> 00:01:02,339
It is called the resonance hybrid.

24
00:01:02,689 --> 00:01:05,573
No single drawing shows the real molecule.

25
00:01:05,573 --> 00:01:07,177
Only the hybrid does.

26
00:01:07,827 --> 00:01:10,575
Let's build ozone on our molecule bench.

27
00:01:10,575 --> 00:01:12,022
Three oxygen atoms.

28
00:01:12,022 --> 00:01:14,561
The middle one bonds to both sides.

29
00:01:14,911 --> 00:01:18,769
In drawing one, the left bond is
double and the right bond is single.

30
00:01:18,769 --> 00:01:22,536
The ruler should read one hundred
twenty one picometres on the left, and

31
00:01:22,536 --> 00:01:24,632
one hundred forty eight on the right.

32
00:01:25,032 --> 00:01:26,502
Now watch the electrons.

33
00:01:26,502 --> 00:01:29,599
One pair slides from the
left bond to the right bond.

34
00:01:29,999 --> 00:01:31,333
This is drawing two.

35
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:34,752
Now the right bond is double
and the left bond is single.

36
00:01:34,752 --> 00:01:36,811
Same atoms, only electrons moved.

37
00:01:37,212 --> 00:01:41,021
But when chemists measure real ozone,
both bonds are one hundred twenty

38
00:01:41,021 --> 00:01:42,073
eight picometres.

39
00:01:42,473 --> 00:01:46,808
One hundred twenty eight sits between
one hundred twenty one and one hundred

40
00:01:46,808 --> 00:01:47,716
forty eight.

41
00:01:47,716 --> 00:01:50,759
Each bond is between a
single and a double bond.

42
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:53,395
So the real ozone is the hybrid.

43
00:01:53,395 --> 00:01:57,659
Drawing one and drawing two are
only ways to describe it on paper.

44
00:01:58,309 --> 00:02:00,409
Compare the two drawings side by side.

45
00:02:00,409 --> 00:02:02,624
Mirror images, only the electrons moved.

46
00:02:02,974 --> 00:02:04,036
Pause and think.

47
00:02:04,036 --> 00:02:07,406
Does ozone keep flipping between
drawing one and drawing two?

48
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:11,506
No!

49
00:02:11,042 --> 00:02:14,008
Green paint never flips
between blue and yellow.

50
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,809
Ozone is always the hybrid.

51
00:02:16,459 --> 00:02:17,863
Now a bigger case.

52
00:02:17,863 --> 00:02:20,822
The carbonate ion, CO three, two minus.

53
00:02:20,822 --> 00:02:21,913
Step by step.

54
00:02:22,263 --> 00:02:23,163
Step one.

55
00:02:22,994 --> 00:02:26,481
Carbon sits in the middle with
three oxygen atoms around it.

56
00:02:27,231 --> 00:02:28,131
Step two.

57
00:02:27,965 --> 00:02:31,096
One drawing has one double
bond and two single bonds.

58
00:02:31,096 --> 00:02:33,906
That predicts one short
bond and two long ones.

59
00:02:34,656 --> 00:02:35,556
Step three.

60
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:37,964
The double bond can sit on
any of the three oxygens.

61
00:02:37,964 --> 00:02:39,420
So there are three drawings.

62
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:41,070
Step four.

63
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:44,255
Experiments show all three
carbon oxygen bonds are equal.

64
00:02:44,255 --> 00:02:46,783
The real ion is the hybrid of all three.

65
00:02:47,533 --> 00:02:49,700
The hybrid is also more stable.

66
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:53,523
Its energy is lower than the
energy of any single drawing.

67
00:02:53,523 --> 00:02:56,303
So resonance makes a molecule more stable.

68
00:02:57,053 --> 00:02:59,403
Carbon dioxide also shows resonance.

69
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:03,973
Its carbon oxygen bond is one hundred
fifteen picometres, between a double

70
00:03:03,973 --> 00:03:08,494
bond, one hundred twenty one, and
a triple bond, one hundred ten.

71
00:03:09,144 --> 00:03:10,160
Remember this.

72
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,257
The real molecule is the hybrid.

73
00:03:12,257 --> 00:03:13,918
A blend, never a flip.

74
00:03:14,618 --> 00:03:16,308
Now, one worked example.

75
00:03:16,608 --> 00:03:21,265
What is the bond order of each carbon
oxygen bond in the carbonate ion?

76
00:03:21,765 --> 00:03:24,304
In any one drawing, count the bonds.

77
00:03:24,304 --> 00:03:28,225
One double bond is two, plus
two single bonds is two more.

78
00:03:28,225 --> 00:03:29,697
Four bonds in total.

79
00:03:30,447 --> 00:03:34,654
These four bonds are shared equally
by three carbon oxygen links.

80
00:03:35,404 --> 00:03:38,363
Four divided by three is
one point three three.

81
00:03:38,363 --> 00:03:42,293
Each bond is a little more than
single, much less than double.

82
00:03:42,943 --> 00:03:44,405
Now, the exam trap.

83
00:03:44,755 --> 00:03:48,757
Some students think ozone stays in
drawing one for some time, then jumps

84
00:03:48,757 --> 00:03:49,800
to drawing two.

85
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,100
Wrong.

86
00:03:50,723 --> 00:03:53,021
The drawings do not exist on their own.

87
00:03:53,021 --> 00:03:55,799
There is no flipping and
no balance between them.

88
00:03:55,799 --> 00:03:59,640
Ozone is always the hybrid, with both
bonds at one hundred twenty eight

89
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,540
picometres.

90
00:04:01,027 --> 00:04:02,386
Where is this asked?

91
00:04:02,386 --> 00:04:06,491
Questions on resonance structures,
bond order by resonance, and comparing

92
00:04:06,491 --> 00:04:07,422
bond lengths.

93
00:04:08,022 --> 00:04:09,297
Exam level now.

94
00:04:09,297 --> 00:04:14,386
Which order of carbon oxygen bond
length is correct for CO, CO two and

95
00:04:14,386 --> 00:04:15,823
the carbonate ion?

96
00:04:15,823 --> 00:04:17,152
Pause and solve.

97
00:04:22,552 --> 00:04:23,998
The answer is A.

98
00:04:23,998 --> 00:04:27,753
CO is shortest, then
CO two, then carbonate.

99
00:04:28,253 --> 00:04:31,353
CO has a triple bond, bond order three.

100
00:04:31,353 --> 00:04:33,520
CO two has bond order two.

101
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,776
Carbonate shares four
bonds over three links.

102
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,908
Bond order one point three three.

103
00:04:39,408 --> 00:04:41,919
Higher bond order means a shorter bond.

104
00:04:41,919 --> 00:04:44,333
So the carbonate bond is the longest.

105
00:04:44,933 --> 00:04:46,473
Here is your recap.

106
00:04:46,473 --> 00:04:48,056
Screenshot this card.

107
00:04:51,256 --> 00:04:53,442
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

108
00:04:53,842 --> 00:04:54,742
One.

109
00:04:54,288 --> 00:04:56,902
Why are both bonds in
ozone the same length?

110
00:04:57,702 --> 00:04:58,602
Two.

111
00:04:58,135 --> 00:05:01,265
How many resonance structures
does the carbonate ion have?

112
00:05:02,065 --> 00:05:02,965
Three.

113
00:05:02,584 --> 00:05:05,865
Why is a resonance hybrid more
stable than any one drawing?

114
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:11,915
Next time: why does water have a plus
end and a minus end, but carbon dioxide

115
00:05:11,915 --> 00:05:12,815
does not?

116
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:16,211
We find out in polarity of
bonds and dipole moment.
